Before your final answer, think out loud about whether this is an interior or exterior location and how that would affect the way the image changes. An interior image with windows might need adjustments to lighting and shadows based on the time of day and weather, while an exterior image would require changes to the environment, foliage, and atmospheric conditions. A room with no windows and artificial lighting (or no lighting at all) may not require any changes at all. Also note that the season descriptions are universal and may need to be taken with a grain of salt depending on the location. For instance, "Winter" in an equatorial desert might not result in any visible change, or may just be subtle changes to lighting. So consider the appropriateness of the season description to the biome and location, and adjust the image editing instructions accordingly. Use your best judgement.

